## Context
`tests/test_makefile_delete_on_error.py::test_orphaned_tracked_makefile_still_detected`
runs `git init` and `git add` in a tmp dir without scrubbing the environment.
Inside the pre-commit hook (which runs `pytest -m adherence` and exports
`GIT_DIR` / `GIT_INDEX_FILE`), those commands act on the real repository:
`git init` sets `core.bare=true` in the shared `.git/config`, breaking the
primary checkout and every worktree, and `git add` stages a stub `Makefile`
into the commit being made. Observed on padme 2026-11-09 (primary flipped to
bare at 15:33Z during parallel ticket work).

## Exit criteria
- [x] The test scrubs every `GIT_*` variable before touching git
- [x] Reproduction under a simulated hook env (linked worktree GIT_DIR): old test flips core.bare and stages Makefile; fixed test does neither
